This experiment focuses on adapting a pre-trained language model to a specific domain using fine-tuning. A small domain-specific dataset is prepared and used to train the model so that it can generate more relevant and specialized responses. The fine-tuned model is then evaluated using sample questions and compared with the original model.

Technologies: Python, Ollama, Llama 3.2, Hugging Face Transformers

Workflow:
Domain Dataset
      ↓
Data Preparation
      ↓
Pre-trained LLM
      ↓
Fine-Tuning
      ↓
Specialized Model
      ↓
Testing & Evaluation
      ↓
Compare Original vs Fine-Tuned Model

Objective:
To understand how fine-tuning can improve an LLM's performance for a specific domain or task.
